==Spanish==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[nonbre]] (''obsolete'')

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|es}} {{term|nomen|nōmen|lang=la}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|h₁nḗh₃mn̥|lang=es}}.

===Noun===
{{es-noun-m}}

# [[name]]
#: ''¿Cuál es tu '''nombre'''?'' — “What is your name?”
#: ''Mi '''nombre''' es ‘Carlos’.'' — “My name is ‘Carlos’.”

====Usage notes====
In Spanish, it is a bit more common to use {{term|llamar|llamarse|to be called}} to indicate someone’s name:
: ''¿Cómo te llamas?'' — “What is your name.” (Literally, “How are you called?”)
: ''Me llamo ‘Carlos’.'' — “My name is ‘Carlos’.” (Literally, “I am called ‘Carlos’.”)

